  data: {
    LLM: "Play honestly when possible to avoid getting caught. Challenge when you are certain someone is bluffing based on card counting. Don't challenge too often or you'll end up taking piles.\n\nCount cards to know what ranks have been played. Bluff strategically when you have many cards of a rank that has already passed. Watch opponents' patterns - some players always bluff on certain ranks.\n\nSophisticated bluffing patterns that are hard to read. Psychological manipulation through false tells. Optimal challenge timing based on probability and game state. Managing hand composition for endgame.",
